{#
_partials/_sender_picture.html.twig — the sender picture inside an avatar
circle (#639), as two macros the circle's own markup calls.

  attributes(address, verified, picture)
      What the circle carries for the live update (mail--sender-pictures):
      the keys SenderPictureNotifier names rows by, whether this message
      passed the sender check (only that admits a BIMI logo), and the rank of
      the picture it already shows, 99 for initials. A later picture replaces
      this one only if it ranks better.

  image(picture)
      The <img> itself, over the initial, or nothing when picture is null.

Macros rather than an include because both halves belong INSIDE markup the
caller owns — the attributes on its circle, the image in its body — and the
row's circle doubles as its checkbox label, which no partial should redraw.

The initial stays underneath the image. If the picture ever fails to load,
the alt text is empty, so the broken image paints nothing and the initial
shows through.
#}
{% macro attributes(address, verified, picture) %}
    {%- set keys = sender_picture_keys(address) -%}
    data-sender-picture
    data-sender-picture-rank="{{ picture ? picture.rank : 99 }}"
    data-sender-verified="{{ verified ? '1' : '0' }}"
    {%- if keys.address %} data-sender-picture-address="{{ keys.address }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if keys.domain %} data-sender-picture-domain="{{ keys.domain }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if keys.site %} data-sender-picture-site="{{ keys.site }}"{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro image(picture) %}
    {%- if picture -%}
        <img src="{{ path('app_sender_picture', { reference: picture.reference }) }}"
             alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" draggable="false"
             data-sender-picture-image
             class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full rounded-full object-cover bg-surface">
    {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
